The '''Shwuy Exchange''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that went between the astronomical objects [[Uviuy Exen]] and [[Vakkar]] in the [[Colonies]] region.<ref name="Where" /> It passed through the [[Shwuy sector|Shwuy]] and [[Fakir sector]]s.<ref name="Sectors" /> From Uviuy Exen, which lay on the [[Hydian Way]]<ref name="Galaxy">{{StarWarsGalaxyMap}}</ref> [[super-hyperroute]],<ref name="BMF 48">{{BuildFalconCite|48|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> the route went to the [[Mefti system|Mefti]] and [[Thrinittik system]]s,<ref name="Galaxy" /> and then to<ref name="CLNE" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Identity Crisis">{{TBB|Identity Crisis}}</ref> [[Caraad]]<ref name="CLNE" /> before it reached the [[Palanhi system]],<ref name="Galaxy" /> which acted as a junction onto the [[Namadii Corridor]].<ref name="Namadii" /> After Palanhi, the route terminated at the [[Vakkar system]], where one had to use local astrocartographers and smugglers to travel anywhere beyond.<ref name="Where" /> The route passed through [[Standard Galactic Grid]] squares K-9, K-8, L-8, and L-9.<ref name="Galaxy" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Schwuy Exchange was first depicted in the [[The galaxy|galactic]] [[map]] in [[Fantasy Flight Games]]' [[2016]] [[canon]] roleplaying supplement [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]].<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> It was then identified in the [[StarWars.com]] article [[Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Rogue One?|Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Rogue One''?]], published on [[January 31]] [[2017]].<ref name="Where" />

